      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1328517567,
      "text": "Cordia alliodora is a species of flowering tree in the family Cordiaceae, that is native to the American tropics. It is commonly known as Spanish elm, Ecuador laurel, cypre or salmwood. It can reach 35 m in height."
    },
    "es": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (es): Cordia alliodora",
